        <head>WBEN THE LIVER'S WRONG</head>
        <p>WBEN THE LIVER'S WRONG</p>
        <p>Everything else seems to go wrong. While the body is suffering, the mind also becomes depressed; and while the complexion is getting sallower, the breath shorter. the tongue more furred and the blood more feverish, the eyes, which are already tinged with yellow and more or less bloodshot, look out upon life with the very dreariest and most ill-humoured sensations. Not much patience goes to the constitutidn of an habitually " liv cry " per- son; but it is nevertheless a fact that much evil is due to what may be called "impatient," haphazard, and excessive dosing with pills and draughs which have an injurious effect upon the liver, tending to confirm the sluggish habit of the body and gradually leading to in- creased doses that finally have a most pernicious and ever. permanently bad effect upon a really very delicate organ—though the liver is not usually thought to be so. , This is a state of things which has been and still is the cause of many a serious illness, and in some cases of fatal decline. More enlightPned methors, however, now prevail, and the treatment of habitual constipation, sluggish liver, bilis •usness, and all the other everyday ills arising from a disordered condition of the liver and bowels, by the use of the ori- ginal, genuine California Syrup of Figs has proved more picc-ssful than any other. Syrop of Figs is a cl,licious liquid laxative preparation made from the finest ripe figs.in combination with other valuable vegetable AO-- stances whose properties are known to be medicinally laxative. It acts so gently and soothingly upon liver, kidneys.and bowels,and is so prompt in its results,caus- ing no discomfort or inconvenience whatever, that it may 103 safely ranked as the most successful aperimt remed.7 known ,to medical science. flealth, appetite, energv.an4 good 'spirits are the blessings that follow tho nse of Syrup of Figs. Remember the words " Syrup of Figs "do not alone constitute a guarantee of genuine- nes,. You must ask fcr " 