        <p>THE SLEEPING-OUT NUISANCE.—On SltUrday merning, at the Rtincorn Police Cove, before Messrs. F. J. Norman and S. Taylor, a loafer, named George bolt, was charged with sleeping in an ont-building belonging to the Salt Union Limited, at Weston Point, without having. any visible means of subsistance.—Sergeant Brewster explained that the prisoner had been twice ejected from the stables of the Bridgewater Trustees during the week—Having previous convictions recorded [against- him, liolt was sent •to Knutsford for 21 days' I hard labour.</p>
