        <p>Vrospertus. _ The SUB3CRIPTION LIST will OPEN ON THURSDAY the 3rd of December, 1896, and will be CLOSED st or before 4 pan. FRIDAY, DECH ABER 4TE, for London and Coun ry. PARR'S BANK (LIMITED). Bartholomew-lane, London, ICC., and Cook-street, Liverpool, and their Branches, (snd their agents Guinees, Mahon. and Co • 17 College Green, Dublin), authorised to RECEIVE SUBSCRIPTIONS for the under-mentioned ISSUE of DEBENTURE STOCK and PREFERENCE SHARES. 'TIIE WEST CHESHIRE BREWERY COMPANY L (Limited).—(Messrs. Gatehouse and Son (Limited), Irrkenhead). Incorporated under the Companies Acts, 162 to 1893. SHARE CAPITAL. 12,000 Five per Cent. Cumulative Preference Shares of £lO each £121.000 8,000 Ordinary Shares of £lO each BO,OOO -- Making a total capital of The whole of the Ordinary Shares, ad £2D,000 of the Pre- ference Shares, are taken by Gatehouse and Son (Limited) (the Shareholders in which are Messrs. Gatehouse and room- hers of their family), in part payment to them of the pur- chase money payable under the contract for sale. The Pre- ference Shares confer the right to a fixed Cumulative Pre- terential Dividend at the rate of £5 per cent. per annum,and the right to repayment of Capital in priority to the Ordinary Shares, but do not confer on the holders the right to attend or vote, either in person or by proxy, at any General Meeting unless the Dividendupon the said shares or any of them is one month in arrear. or the Meeting is convened for increas- ing or reducing the Capital or winding up, or sanctioning a sale of the undertaking, or altering the regulations of the Company. or where the preposition to be submitted to the meeting directly affects the rights and privileges of the Pre ference Shareholders. Irredeemable £4 per Cent. First Mortgage, Debenture Stock £131,000 The alove Stock will be secureii by a First Mortgage to Trustees of the whole of the Freehold and Leasehold Proper- ties owned by the Company, coupled with a floating first charge on all its other assets, according to the provisiona con- tained in the draft trust, deed mentioned below. ISSUE of £13:1,000 FOUR PER CENT. IRREDEEMABLE FIRST MORTGAGE DEBENTURE' STOCK at par, issued in amounts of not less than £5O, and above that amount in multiples af £lO ; and 10,000 FIVE PER CENT. CUMULATIVE PREFERENCE SHARES of £lO each at par. The payments are to be made as follows :- 1 DE BENT URE STOCK, SHARES. £lO percent. on Application. £1 per Share on Application. £4O per cent. on Allotment. £5 per Share on Allotment. £5O per cent. two months £4 per Share two months after Allotment. after Allotment. £lOO £lO Payment may be made in tull on Allotment. under dl.- count at 4 per cent. per annum ; failure to pay any instal- meta will render previous instalments liable to forfeitore. The interest on the Debenture Stock and the Dividend on the Preference Shares will be payable half yearly in the months of January and July. TRUSTEES FOR THE DEBENTURE STOCK lIOLDERS.—The Law Guarantee and Trust Society (Limited). 41, Chancery-lane, London, E.C. DIRECTORS. Che, les Gatehouse. ) Directors of Gatehouse Richard George Gatehouse, and Son (Limited), William Robert Russell, BANKERS.— Parr's Bank (Limiteil), Bartholornew-lane,Londen, C , and Cook-street, Liverpool, and their Branches, SOLICITORS—F. J. Leslie and Co., lb, Union-court, Castle. street. Liverpool. BROKERS. londen.—Stephen C. Cork and Sou, 6, Drapers' garden, Ex., and Stock Exchange Liverpool —Aocatta and Brown, 17, Sweeting-street. and Liver. 00l Stock Exchange. luniroßs.—Chalmers, Wade. and Coachartered accountants 5, Fenwick-street.Liverpeol, and 18. Queen Victoria-street London, B.C. SE,JRETARY and Registered Offioes— J. A. Bland, Queen's Brewery, Tranmere, Birkenhead. PROSPECTUS. This Company is. an extension of Gatehouse and Son (Limited). br-wers. of Tranmere, Birtsenhead, Cheshire. The business, which bears a high reput non, has been established for many years, and is a profitable and steadily progres- sive one. The Brewery, which is freehold, is substantially built and has recently been refitted, and is in good order thoughout, and well adapted for carrying on au extensive trade. The present Company is incorporated for the purpose of develop- ing and enlarging the business and to provide funds for the acquisition of additional properties. The Company will acquire free from encumbrance The Freehold Brewery and Laud, together with fixed plant, horses, carts, casks, ,te. 50 Freehold Licensed Houses. 16 Leasehold Licensed Houses, and one on annual tenancy. 95 Freeho d Shops and Horses, all of which adjoin the Brewery or the Licensed Pro, erties above-mentioned are in a good state of repair, and well let. The whole of the above Properties, with the exception o two only, are within cartage distance of the Brewery. The Company employs no Managers in any of its Licensed Houses, the whole being let to bona-fide tenants. The Business will be carried on by the existing Staff, and all the Directors of Gatehouse and Son (Limited) will be Directors of the new Company. The steadily progressive character of the business is shown by the following certificate of Messrs. Chalmers, Wade and Co.. who have regularly audited the books for the last eight years : "To the Directors of the WEST CHESHIRE BREWERY COMPANY (Limited), ku-istreet,udltaudited Liverpool,tek o t hooks November. Messrs. GlaBt9e3hmuse. " 5F We haveen wr gy d h and Son, Brewers. Birkenhead, and their successors, Gate- house and Son (Limited), for the past eight years. "The business has steadily progressed, and we certify that the net profits, inelnding the rentals, after providing for depreciation and bad debts, but before charging Debenture interest and Directors fees, were as follows For the year ended 30th June, )694 £11,597 11 8 1a95 14,062 8 7 For the 15 months ended 30th Septemher, 1896 21,890 13 2 Being. for the past fifteen months, at the rate of £17,512 108 61 psr annum. " The above profits are on the sale of ale and beer alone, the Company not having so far exercisel its right to supply to its tenants wines and spirits, which, if now exercised, should be an addition to the profit-earning trade of the Company. " We understand that it is intended to provide 20,:00/. additional working capital for investment in the business, which should further considerably add to its profits. "CHALMERS, WADE.ancl Co., Chartered Accountants." On a low estimate, the profits accruing from the supply to the tied houses of wines and spirits should, in the opinion of the Directors, amount to at least £2,0e0 per annum. The additional £20,000 working capital provided by this Issue. if invested to realise only 5 per cent., will produce a further sum of £lllOO per annnm.£67oo of this £20,010 will be applied to the payment of the baiance due on the New Ferry Hotel, included in Mr. Thomson's valuation,but the purchase of which has not yet been completed The certified profits of the last fifteen months amount to the sum of £21,890 13s. 2d., which is at the rate of £17,512 10s. 61 per annum ... £17,512 10 6 To pay Interest ors £l3O 000 £4 per cent. Debenture Stock requires 6 per cent, dividend upon £120,000 £5 per eent. Cumulative Preference Shares NCO 11,201 0 0 6,312 10 6 To this balance of £6312 las. 6d. must be added the sums of £2OOO and £loi.o men- tioned above</p>
        <p>Making a total suns of £9,312 JO 6 which world be available for Divideud on the Ordinary Shares, Directors' Fees, &amp;c. It will be observed that the certified earnings of the Com- pany are more than sufficient to pay the interest on the De- benture Stoci three times over, and that after paying the interest en the Debenture Stock the Dividend on the Prefer- ence Shares is enore than twice covered. Mr. %Vilna:a Thomson, the well-knowa brewery valuer of Liverpool, has recently made a valuation of the properties to he acquired by the Company, of which the following is acopy. Front this it will be seen that the assets, exclu ling the very valuable goodwill attaching to the Brewery, except as to family and free trade, amount to £196,220, To this sum must be added the unappropriated balanee of the £eo,ooo provided for additional working capital, making a total of assets of £299,520. "T. the Directors of the WEST CHESHIRE BREWERY COMPANY (Limited), " 7. Cook-street. Liverpool 21st November, 1896. " I have inspected the Freehold Brewery Premises situate at Tranmere, near Birkenhead, belonging to Messrs. Gate- house and Son (Limit. d), togetlir with the fixed and move- able plant, stock and materials there also the licensed houses, I trade fixtures and fittings, and other Freehold and Le rseheld I Properties situate in Birkenhead and Chester Districts, Elles- mere Port, New Brighton, Seacombe, wed Liverpool, as per Schedule annexed hereto, which I value (exclosive of good- will attaching to the Brewery except as to family and free trade) et the sum of One hundred and ninety-six thousand I two hundred and twenty pounds (say £196.220), as under 'The Brewery at Tranmere, with the fixed plant; the 50 Licensed Premises, nll being Freehold; the 95 Freehold Unlicensed Prembes, which adjoin the Licensed Premises and areconvenient to be held therewith £156,445 "The benefit in the leases of 17 Licensed Houses ' and Property adjoining held on leases, with the ex- ception of one wh ch is held on yearly teoancy " The railing stove, casks, horses, cirts, fixtures in Houees, and other sundry assets of the business, in- cluding the brewery profit in respect of the family and tree trade "The stock-in-trade of raw and manufactured goods, taken at or below cost, on the 30th September, 1896 " I have received a certificate from Messrs. Chal- mers, Wade. and Co ' chartered accountants, Liver- pool. 'that the bookdebts, after making provision for discount and bad and doubtful debts, are, in our opinion, worth £7374 18s, lid.' 7,374 " Thus making the total amount of my valuation the sum of £196,2?.0 " The above properties are in a good state of repair. and have been well selected for the continuance and development of toe trade. " WM. THOMSON, Valuer and Property Auctioneer." The price to be paid to the Vendors for the business,and all the assets ionnected therewith, and which are comprised in the above valuation of Mr. *William Thomson together with the valuable goodwill atteching to the Brewery, has been fixed at the sum of £,310,C00, payable as to £BO,OOO in Ordiu</p>
        <p>ary Shares of the Company, £20,C00 in Preference Shares and the balance in cash, The Vendors pay all the expenses of incorporation of the Company, and the issue of its capital down to Allotment. The following Contracts have been entered into—(l) Dated 20th October, 1896, between Gatehouse and Son (Limited) and James Rupert Campbell and John Crowther, herein called Vendors ; (2) Dated 21st November, 1896, between the Vendors and this Company, for the re-sale at a profit of the properties and assets acquired by them under the first Coatract. In addition to the Contracts above-mentioned, there are Agreements entered Into by the old Company since its incor- peration in the ordinary course of carrying on its business, sea there are Contracts for the guarantee of a portion of the capital now offered, to which latter the Company is not a party. All applicants for the Stock and Shares will be deemed to have waived any rights to further particulars et contracts, whether under section ift ef " The Companies Act, 1867." or otherwise ; and to have agreed with the Company, as Trustees fo: the Directors, the Trustees, and all persons authorising or takiag part in the issue of this Prospectus, not to make any claim upon them, or any of them, under the said Section. or upon any other ground except wilful misstatement. and Allotments will only be made upon this condition. Fhe draft of the Trust Deed vor securing the Debenture Stock, the abov--mentioned Contracts, the valuation et Mr. af. Thomson, the Certificate of Messrs. Chalmers, Wade and Co.. and copies of the Memorandum and Articles of Associa- tion. can be inspected by applicants for Shares and Stock at the ffices of the Company's Solicitors. It is intended to apply in due course for an official quota- tion for the Debenture Stock and Preference Shares on the London and Liverpool Stock Exchanges. Application should be made on the following forms, or the forma accompanying the Prospectus, and forwarded to the Bankers