        <p>GOOD TEMPLARY AT LATC#IFORD. The weekly meeting of the Latchford Good Templars (Bonehill Branch Lodge) was held in the Temperance Hall on Monday evening, Bro. H. Flecher, C. T., presiding. There was a good attend- ance. The programme for the evening consisted of a paper by Bro. J. Ditchfield, entitled " Our aim in life." Bro. A. Ford moved a vote of thanks to the essayist, Bro. L. Ellison seconded, and Bros. E. Cliff. W. Pearson. F. A. Jenkins, J. J. Corbett, and the Chairman supported the proposition, all of whom spoke in high terms of the paper. Bro. J. Ditch- field suitably responded.</p>
